title: The Chemnitz Conference
subtitle: The signal for the rising is to be given at a workers' conference.
new-page: true
tags: rf_event
view-if: year = 1923 and month >= 10 and saxony_seen = 1
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.chemnitz_seen = 1;
Q.october_leader = Q.leader;
Q.october_leader_name = window.RF.names[Q.leader];
!}

= The Chemnitz Conference

On 21 October a conference of factory councils, unions and workers' parties meets in Chemnitz. [? if october_plan : The plan is for the <span class="p-kpd">KPD</span> to propose a general strike there, as the signal for the rising. ?][? if october_plan = 0 : Moscow's plan was postponed, but the question of a general strike is on the agenda anyway. ?] Without the left <span class="p-spd">SPD</span>, the strike will be a Communist affair alone.

[? if spd_relation >= 60 : The left <span class="p-spd">SPD</span> delegates are listening. Some of them might follow. ?][? if spd_relation < 60 : The <span class="p-spd">SPD</span> delegates, led by Labour Minister Georg Graupe, make clear they will walk out if the <span class="p-kpd">KPD</span> proposes a general strike. ?]

Readiness: [+ readiness +]. Revolutionary situation: [+ rev_situation +]. Union influence: [+ union_influence +]. Relations with the <span class="p-spd">SPD</span>: [+ spd_relation +].

- @call_strike
- @retreat

@call_strike
title: Call the general strike. This is the moment.
subtitle: Pleases the <span class="f-left">Left</span>, <span class="f-ultra">Ultra-Left</span> and <span class="f-stalin">Thälmann</span>. Angers the <span class="f-right">Right</span>. Everything depends on the rising.
on-arrival: {!
Q.chemnitz_strike = 1;
window.RF.lean(Q, {left: 4, ultra: 3, stalin: 2, right: -4});
!}
go-to: rising

@retreat
title: Withdraw the proposal. Live to fight another day.
subtitle: Pleases the <span class="f-right">Right</span> and <span class="f-center">Middle Group</span>. Angers the <span class="f-left">Left</span>, <span class="f-ultra">Ultra-Left</span> and <span class="f-stalin">Thälmann</span>.
on-arrival: {!
Q.chemnitz_strike = 0;
Q.october_outcome = 'retreat';
window.RF.lean(Q, {right: 3, center: 3, left: -5, ultra: -5, stalin: -3});
!}
go-to: retreated

@rising
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
Q.rising_won = window.RF.rising(Q) ? 1 : 0;
!}
go-to: won if rising_won = 1; crushed if rising_won = 0

@won
on-arrival: rf_over = 1; rf_ending = "revolution"

= The general strike

The conference votes for the general strike. Saxony and Thuringia stop. The Proletarian Hundreds take the police stations and arsenals the plan named. In Berlin, the Ruhr and Hamburg the factories empty, and enough of the <span class="p-spd">SPD</span>'s members come out that their leaders cannot hold them back. When the <span class="p-reichswehr">Reichswehr</span> marches on Saxony, it finds railwaymen who will not move its trains and soldiers who will not shoot.

(Rising: [+ rising_score +] against the [+ rising_needed +] needed.)

@crushed
on-arrival: {!
Q.october_outcome = 'crushed';
Q.members = Math.round(Q.members * 0.6);
Q.readiness = 0;
Q.repression += 40;
Q.spd_relation -= 15;
Q.union_influence -= 15;
Q.rev_situation -= 25;
Q.party_banned = 1;
Q[Q.leader + '_moscow'] -= 10;
Q[Q.leader + '_dissent'] += 15;
!}

= The rising fails

The strike is called, but the <span class="p-spd">SPD</span>'s workers stay at work. Where the Hundreds rise, they are isolated in a few towns. The <span class="p-reichswehr">Reichswehr</span> moves into Saxony and Thuringia. Within days the leaders are arrested or in hiding, the party offices are closed, and the government bans the <span class="p-kpd">KPD</span>.

(Rising: [+ rising_score +] against the [+ rising_needed +] needed.)

@retreated

= The retreat

The <span class="p-kpd">KPD</span> withdraws its proposal. The conference refers the question to a commission, which is a polite way of burying it. Couriers are sent across the country to call off the rising.
